From 5d7b8df3acc3898d22f955ba89abec5ec98d3024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VideoPlayerGold snapshot <jestar001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:45:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vf_vsrhost: GPU-resident video super-resolution through a
 runtime host library

Push/pull plumbing for multi-frame super-resolution hosts: CUDA nv12 in, a
larger CUDA nv12 frame out (BT.709) from an own pool, input read ahead of
output demand and released once the host has copied it, output pts taken
from the input frame with the same serial, EOF drained, reset on seek,
fail-open. The network lives in a host library loaded at runtime across
the C ABI in vsrhost.h.
