index 0000000000..fcedf2aec2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/video/filter/vf_vsrhost.c
@@ -0,0 +1,815 @@
+/*
+ * vf_vsrhost: GPU-resident video super-resolution through a host library (CUDA)
+ *
+ * Plumbing only: CUDA nv12 frames in, a larger CUDA nv12 frame out (BT.709),
+ * frames never leave GPU memory. The network, its colour conversion and its
+ * multi-frame latency live in a host library loaded at runtime across the C
+ * ABI in vsrhost.h, so no vendor SDK links into mpv.
+ *
+ * Unlike vf_dlssnr this filter is push/pull: the host holds a chunk of input
+ * frames (about 28) before the first output appears, so input is read ahead
+ * of output demand (as vf_vapoursynth does), each input surface is released
+ * as soon as the host has copied it, and output pts come from the input
+ * frame with the same serial.
+ *
+ * Input: anything decodable is converted to CUDA nv12 in front (autoconvert, as refqueue does), so
+ * 10-bit and software-decoded SD sources work too.
+ *
+ * Fail-open: a missing host, a host that refuses the stream (HD, HDR, odd
+ * aspect, missing engines) or a push failure plays the original picture with
+ * one warning.
+ *
+ * Runtime: `vf-command <label> enable <yes|no>`.
+ *
+ * This file is part of mpv.
+ *
+ * mpv is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
+ * modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public
+ * License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either
+ * version 2.1 of the License, or (at your option) any later version.
+ *
+ * mpv is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
+ * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
+ * MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
+ * GNU Lesser General Public License for more details.
+ *
